attempts.analysis:
**What actually happened:** The LP oracle confirms the incumbent is an *exact* local optimum of its basin — my 523s of kick→climb evaluation never found a better one. Not one improvement after t=0. The defect is in acceptance economics:

1. **`sweepStep`/`swapMove` judge the *immediate* LP value of a teleport/swap (`v > v0 + 3e-7`)**, which in a saturated packing is *always* terrible (teleported circle lands in a hole of clearance ≪ r_i). Basin-crossing moves are rejected before the climb that would reveal their post-rearrangement value. I reproduced the premature-rejection failure I had diagnosed in the previous program.
2. **Greedy-only acceptance everywhere.** `probeV`/`hillClimb` only accept strict improvements, so the search can never *descend* out of the record basin — it can only find an *adjacent better* basin, and the log shows those gains come at ~1e-3/kick rate. With climbs costing 0.2–1.7s, I got only a few hundred trials.
3. **No simulated annealing.** Both published record runs (AlphaEvolve, ShinkaEvolve) used SA for global escape; my program has none. SA directly on the exact LP value V(centers) — never tried — gives ~2.5ms Metropolis steps instead of 500ms climb trials, i.e. orders of magnitude more barrier-crossing attempts.

**Fix (targeted, keeping the LP machinery that produced 2.635902998 and its repair/finalize untouched):**
- `sweepStep`/`swapMove`: accept when within tolerance of v0 (`−2.5e-3`, `−1.2e-3`), then *always* hill-climb and compare post-climb value — evaluate the destination, not the doorstep.
- New `saRun`: true Metropolis over the exact LP value (gaussian/teleport/swap/band-rotate/scale proposals, T annealed ~1e-3→1e-5), starting ~62% from global best, 26% from elites; deep-climb only when raw V comes within 8e-5 of the record *and* exceeds the last climbed value (suppresses re-climbing the same basin). ~69% of main-loop time now goes to SA slices.
- Final phase uses SA slices as the escape when sweeps stagnate.
- Safety: best is banked at t=0 by `considerBest` before anything runs; all new loops are time-guarded; output path unchanged.

