**ANALYSIS**

Checking my assumptions against what actually ran:

1. **The incumbent assumption FAILED.** First trace value is 2.620592502 — if `params` had contained the 2.635907462 packing, init would have scored ≥2.63590. Instead it scored what my no-incumbent branch produces (random + 4s optimize). So this run received no usable start and re-derived everything from random the entire 538s — and still reached 2.635763388, only 1.44e-4 below the incumbent. The optimizer itself works (2.63423 by t=110s is fast for from-scratch). Hardening `extract` is cheap insurance (numeric-string coercion, deeper recursion) but is not the main lever.

2. **The real defect is the schedule, proven by the trace:** 2.634236516 holds from t=110s to t=316s (206s flat), then 2.635763388 holds from t=316s to the end (222s flat). Two ~210s plateaus consumed 78% of the budget with zero conversion. Cause: (a) T decays monotonically to 2.4e-7 — by mid-run the SA accepts almost nothing, and the reheat (`lastImp > 90s && it%10===0`, stuck+12) is far too rare/weak; (b) the `elite` archive only ever stores the chain of record-holders, so the hop target is just `best` wearing different clothes — no basin diversity; hops fire at it%30×0.35 ≈ 1.2% of iterations; (c) after the 2.63576 basin was found at 316s, nothing focused the remaining 222s on micro-perturbing *that* basin with a full-depth optimize — the +1.5e-3 jump at 316s came from a lucky perturb chain, and I have no dedicated mechanism to exploit such finds.

3. **No inverted conditions or placeholder values found** in re-reading; `optimize` strictly decreases energy, `shrinkExact` is monotone, radii stats (min 0.0702, 16 wall-touching, tightest gap = EPS_S exactly) confirm a sane, exactly-repaired near-jammed packing.

Fixes (targeted): cyclic reheat temperature (sawtooth × global decay) so exploration never dies; reheat-to-best every 35s without improvement; true diversity archive (any candidate within 8e-4 of best, dedup by score, cap 12) with much more frequent hopping; a dedicated micro-refine branch (every 17 iters: clone best, tiny perturb, full-depth optimize, always LP-polishable via existing improvement path); slightly more frequent deep dives.

